mongoc-implicit-session-light - an implicit session without the transaction state it cannot use

A command or a cursor with no session of the caller's gets one of the driver's own, an implicit session, made by
mongoc_client_start_session() as an explicit one is: a copy of the client's default transaction options and a
jitter source (the backoff of withTransaction) - neither of which an implicit session ever reads, since it can
start no transaction. _mongoc_client_start_implicit_session() makes the session without them; cmd.c and
cursor.c, the two places that start implicit sessions, call it. mongoc_client_start_session() is unchanged.
_mongoc_client_session_new() takes whether the session is implicit; mongoc_client_session_start_transaction(),
the one reader of the default transaction options, is never called on an implicit session.

Measured (coraine, mongo 8.2.12, user-space instructions per request, perf stat): PATCH -1,829, retrieve -774 (after 0001-0003).

